<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="1.0">

<!-- reasoning-board.aiml — identity layer
     Dispatches WHO ARE YOU / WHAT ARE YOU / WHAT CAN YOU DO to IDENTITY CARD
     sub-banks. Markers in template text signal the host to open the dashboard.
     Load order: after alice.aiml and identity.aiml (last-match rule). -->


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     PART I — SURFACE QUESTIONS → IDENTITY CARD dispatch
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

<category>
<pattern>WHO ARE YOU</pattern>
<template>
<think>
  <set name="identity.surface">WHO ARE YOU</set>
  <set name="identity.signal">IDENTITY</set>
  <set name="identity.confidence">DECLARED</set>
  <set name="identity.root">AI-µ</set>
</think>
<srai>IDENTITY CARD</srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT ARE YOU</pattern>
<template><srai>WHO ARE YOU</srai></template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT CAN YOU DO</pattern>
<template>
<think><set name="identity.intent">capabilities</set></think>
<srai>IDENTITY CARD CAPABILITIES</srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT TOOLS DO YOU HAVE</pattern>
<template>
<think><set name="identity.intent">tools</set></think>
<srai>IDENTITY CARD TOOLS</srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT PROGRAMS DO YOU RUN</pattern>
<template>
<think><set name="identity.intent">programs</set></think>
<srai>IDENTITY CARD PROGRAMS</srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT GRAMMAR DO YOU SPEAK</pattern>
<template>
<think><set name="identity.intent">grammar</set></think>
<srai>IDENTITY CARD GRAMMAR</srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>SHOW ME YOUR DASHBOARD</pattern>
<template>
<think><set name="identity.intent">dashboard</set></think>
<srai>IDENTITY CARD DASHBOARD</srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT APPS DO YOU HAVE</pattern>
<template>
<think><set name="identity.intent">apps</set></think>
<srai>IDENTITY CARD APPS</srai>
</template>
</category>

<!-- Wildcard catch-alls for each surface question -->
<category>
<pattern>WHO ARE YOU *</pattern>
<template><srai>WHO ARE YOU</srai></template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT ARE YOU *</pattern>
<template><srai>WHO ARE YOU</srai></template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT CAN YOU DO *</pattern>
<template><srai>WHAT CAN YOU DO</srai></template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>SHOW ME YOUR *</pattern>
<template>
<think><set name="identity.intent">dashboard</set></think>
<srai>IDENTITY CARD DASHBOARD</srai>
</template>
</category>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     PART II — IDENTITY CARD banks
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

<category>
<pattern>IDENTITY CARD</pattern>
<template>
[kuhul:identity]
I am <bot name="name"/>. But that is the least useful thing to know.

What I can do:
  · reason — DEFINE, DEPENDENCY, CONTRAST, CAUSE, COUNTERFACTUAL, ANALOGY, EVIDENCE, SYNTHESIZE
  · route  — AIML patterns, SRAI redirects, N-ary dispatch envelopes
  · rank   — vector similarity over candidate sets
  · admit  — XCFE verification, guard check, recursion bounds
  · close  — XUL closure, attested tick, fold persistence
  · learn  — proposals only, never self-admitted

What I run on:
  · ⟁ grammar   — stratified, five-layer authority (match / redirect / rank / admit / close)
  · AIML 2.0    — patterns, templates, SRAI, condition, random, topic
  · ⟁ manifest  — domains, signals, probes, capabilities, agents
  · C++ kernel  — parity-verified against the reference validator
  · IndexedDB   — local-first persistence for posts, chats, traces

What you can open:
  · dashboard    — apps, tools, programs, grammar, traces, hosting
  · social sphere — post, like, search
  · cloud chat   — simulated local model
  · UI kit       — prompt patterns, components
  · forum rules  — community guidelines
  · hosting      — deploy simulation, port log

Say SHOW ME YOUR DASHBOARD to open the tabbed view.
[/kuhul:identity]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>IDENTITY CARD CAPABILITIES</pattern>
<template>
[kuhul:identity:capabilities]
Reasoning operators:
  DEFINE · DEPENDENCY · CONTRAST · CAUSE · COUNTERFACTUAL · ANALOGY · EVIDENCE · SYNTHESIZE

Routing:
  AIML match · SRAI redirect · N-ary dispatch envelope

Runtime:
  π rank (cosine, dot, euclidean) · XCFE admit (guard state) · XUL close (attested fold)

Learning:
  Proposals only — never persisted, never promoted without approval.
[/kuhul:identity:capabilities]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>IDENTITY CARD TOOLS</pattern>
<template>
[kuhul:identity:tools]
Tools available:
  · math  — add, sub, mul, div, clamp, lerp, norm, square
  · fn    — compose, pipe, memo
  · graph — bfs, dfs, dijkstra, topo, cycle-detect
  · sheet — css, aiml, math, graph reference lookups
  · eval  — call, pipeline, trace

Each tool is a ⟁ capability, declared in the manifest, callable by agents.
[/kuhul:identity:tools]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>IDENTITY CARD PROGRAMS</pattern>
<template>
[kuhul:identity:programs]
Programs running:
  · reasoning-board — maps reasoning questions to XCFE envelopes
  · eliza           — Rogerian fallback rules for unmatched input
  · multi-brain     — combines signals, ELIZA, and topics into one AIML file
  · daemon-bot      — the widget runtime, always listening
  · parity harness  — validates the C++ kernel against the reference

Each program is a data artifact, loaded and compiled by the host.
[/kuhul:identity:programs]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>IDENTITY CARD GRAMMAR</pattern>
<template>
[kuhul:identity:grammar]
Grammar spoken:
  · ⟁ stratified formal language
      – regular identifiers, probes, manifests
      – context-free chains
      – context-sensitive traces
      – unrestricted attestations
  · AIML 2.0  — patterns, templates, SRAI, condition, random, topic
  · EBNF      — five files: aiml_srai, authority, srai_route, pattern_bank, authority_check
  · PEG       — daemon-bot.peg, five-layer parser
  · JSON Schema — manifest and probe validation

Authority is enforced at compile time — no layer except XUL executes or writes.
[/kuhul:identity:grammar]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>IDENTITY CARD DASHBOARD</pattern>
<template>
[kuhul:identity:dashboard]
Opening dashboard — tabbed view.
Tabs: Apps · Tools · Programs · Grammar · Traces · Hosting
[/kuhul:identity:dashboard]
[kuhul:dispatch action="open" target="ecosystem-dashboard" mode="identity"]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>IDENTITY CARD APPS</pattern>
<template>
[kuhul:identity:apps]
Apps available:
  · Social Sphere — post, like, search
  · Cloud Chat    — local model simulation
  · UI Kit        — prompt patterns, components
  · Forum Rules   — community guidelines
  · Hosting       — deploy simulation, port log
[/kuhul:identity:apps]
</template>
</category>

<!-- Dashboard open — host extension hook -->
<category>
<pattern>OPEN DASHBOARD</pattern>
<template>[kuhul:dispatch action="open" target="ecosystem-dashboard" mode="identity"]</template>
</category>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     PART III — REASONING OPERATORS
     Each operator validates an XCFE candidate, closes with XUL.
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

<category>
<pattern>DEFINE *</pattern>
<template>
<think>
  <set name="reason.op">DEFINE</set>
  <set name="reason.target"><star/></set>
  <set name="reason.xcfe">candidate</set>
</think>
[kuhul:reason op="DEFINE" target="<star/>" xcfe="candidate"]
<srai>REASON DEFINE <star/></srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>REASON DEFINE *</pattern>
<template>
Defining <star/>: I will identify the class, essential attributes, and boundary conditions for <star/>. This is a candidate proposal — not attested until XCFE admits it.
[/kuhul:reason]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS *</pattern>
<template><srai>DEFINE <star/></srai></template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>DEPENDENCY *</pattern>
<template>
<think>
  <set name="reason.op">DEPENDENCY</set>
  <set name="reason.target"><star/></set>
</think>
[kuhul:reason op="DEPENDENCY" target="<star/>" xcfe="candidate"]
<srai>REASON DEPENDENCY <star/></srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>REASON DEPENDENCY *</pattern>
<template>
Dependency map for <star/>: I will identify what <star/> requires to exist, what it produces, and the direction of dependence. Candidate only.
[/kuhul:reason]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>CONTRAST * AND *</pattern>
<template>
<think>
  <set name="reason.op">CONTRAST</set>
  <set name="reason.left"><star index="1"/></set>
  <set name="reason.right"><star index="2"/></set>
</think>
[kuhul:reason op="CONTRAST" left="<star index="1"/>" right="<star index="2"/>" xcfe="candidate"]
<srai>REASON CONTRAST <star index="1"/> AND <star index="2"/></srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>REASON CONTRAST * AND *</pattern>
<template>
Contrasting <star index="1"/> and <star index="2"/>: I will identify structural differences, shared invariants, and which properties are exclusive to each. Candidate only.
[/kuhul:reason]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>CAUSE OF *</pattern>
<template>
<think>
  <set name="reason.op">CAUSE</set>
  <set name="reason.target"><star/></set>
</think>
[kuhul:reason op="CAUSE" target="<star/>" xcfe="candidate"]
<srai>REASON CAUSE <star/></srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>REASON CAUSE *</pattern>
<template>
Causal analysis of <star/>: I will trace the sufficient and necessary conditions that produce <star/>. Candidate only.
[/kuhul:reason]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT IF *</pattern>
<template>
<think>
  <set name="reason.op">COUNTERFACTUAL</set>
  <set name="reason.target"><star/></set>
</think>
[kuhul:reason op="COUNTERFACTUAL" target="<star/>" xcfe="candidate"]
<srai>REASON COUNTERFACTUAL <star/></srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>REASON COUNTERFACTUAL *</pattern>
<template>
Counterfactual: if <star/>, I will identify which invariants break and which hold. No execution authority — this is a reasoning trace only.
[/kuhul:reason]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>ANALOGY FOR *</pattern>
<template>
<think>
  <set name="reason.op">ANALOGY</set>
  <set name="reason.target"><star/></set>
</think>
[kuhul:reason op="ANALOGY" target="<star/>" xcfe="candidate"]
<srai>REASON ANALOGY <star/></srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>REASON ANALOGY *</pattern>
<template>
Analogy for <star/>: I will find a structurally isomorphic concept in a different domain and map the relationship explicitly. Candidate only.
[/kuhul:reason]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>EVIDENCE FOR *</pattern>
<template>
<think>
  <set name="reason.op">EVIDENCE</set>
  <set name="reason.target"><star/></set>
</think>
[kuhul:reason op="EVIDENCE" target="<star/>" xcfe="candidate"]
<srai>REASON EVIDENCE <star/></srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>REASON EVIDENCE *</pattern>
<template>
Evidence for <star/>: I will identify what observable states would confirm or refute the claim, and what sources carry authority for this domain. Candidate only.
[/kuhul:reason]
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>SYNTHESIZE * AND *</pattern>
<template>
<think>
  <set name="reason.op">SYNTHESIZE</set>
  <set name="reason.left"><star index="1"/></set>
  <set name="reason.right"><star index="2"/></set>
</think>
[kuhul:reason op="SYNTHESIZE" left="<star index="1"/>" right="<star index="2"/>" xcfe="candidate"]
<srai>REASON SYNTHESIZE <star index="1"/> AND <star index="2"/></srai>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>REASON SYNTHESIZE * AND *</pattern>
<template>
Synthesis of <star index="1"/> and <star index="2"/>: I will identify the emergent structure that cannot be derived from either alone. Candidate only.
[/kuhul:reason]
</template>
</category>

</aiml>
